  "narration": "[curious] Imagine a phone reveal so convincing,\nyou forget the company hasn’t actually revealed it.\nThe viral clips show a purple Galaxy S27 Ultra with four cameras.\nBut as of November 13, 2026, the phone and “Cobalt Violet” are still UNCONFIRMED.\nSo what actually surfaced?\n[serious] On November 12, Tom’s Guide reported dummy units, including a supposed Ultra.\nNow, why does that matter?\nA dummy copies the outside of a phone.\nIt doesn’t prove the actual device will look the same.\nAnd with studio lighting and camera processing,\nit’s surprisingly easy to make something that looks like an official reveal.\n[skeptical] But there’s something interesting about those cameras.\nThe dummy units show four rear cameras.\nSounds convincing, right?\nExcept that detail conflicts with other leaks.\nIce Universe even claimed the upper-right camera doesn’t exist.\nAnother rumour suggests Samsung could go with just three lenses,\ndropping a secondary 10MP telephoto.\n[thoughtful] So which phone are you actually looking at?\nRight now, it’s a rumour, not a reveal.\nThe real test is simple: wait for Samsung’s official announcement,\nnot a dummy under studio lights.\nFollow us for more AI and technology updates.\nThe free guide and community link are in the description.\nUntil then, that purple phone is evidence of a leak,\nnot proof of what ships.\n",
